          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            A graded codifferential category is like a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/codifferential+category"} codifferential category
            but where the algebra modality is replaced by a graded algebra modality. Whereas
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi FVec
                    %mi 𝕂
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} FVec_{\mathbb{K}}
            is only a trivial codifferential category, with all the structure equal to zero,
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi FVec
                    %mi 𝕂
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} FVec_{\mathbb{K}}
            is a non-trivial codifferential category.
          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            We will use
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/graded+monads"} graded monads
            with grading in the multiplicative monoid of a commutative
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rig"} rig
          .num_defn
            %h6 Definition
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              be a rig. A
              = succeed "-graded" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
              is given by a family
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
